   "file": "01_ld_leader_insurance.md",
   "text": "# Interview 01 (fictional)\nInterviewee: Rachel M., VP Learning & Development, global insurance carrier, ~9,000 employees\nInterviewer: PM, Uplift\nDate: (mock)\n\nPM: Where are you with AI tools today?\nRachel: We bought four thousand enterprise AI licenses eight months ago. Renewal is in March and finance is asking me what we got for the money. I can tell them how many people logged in. That's it.\n\nPM: What would you want to know instead?\nRachel: Which workflows people actually use it for. Underwriting summaries? Claims letters? Email? If I knew where it sticks, I'd know where to put training. Right now I run the same generic prompt workshop for everyone and attendance is falling.\n\nPM: How do you measure time saved today?\nRachel: A self-reported survey. People either ignore it or say \"it saves me five hours a week,\" which nobody believes. I need something credible enough to put in front of the CFO.\n\nPM: Who are your best users?\nRachel: I hear names anecdotally. There's a claims team in Ohio that apparently built their own prompt library. I found out by accident. I'd love to find those people systematically and turn them into champions.\n\nPM: Any concerns?\nRachel: Our employee council will push back hard on anything that looks like monitoring individuals. If this turns into \"the AI is watching you,\" adoption goes down, not up.\n"
