   "file": "02_vp_product_saas.md",
   "text": "# Interview 02 (fictional)\nInterviewee: Tom K., VP Product, B2B software company, ~120 product managers across 6 business units\nInterviewer: PM, Uplift\nDate: (mock)\n\nPM: How are your product managers using AI?\nTom: Wildly unevenly. Maybe fifteen of them have built real workflows: research synthesis, PRD drafts, ticket breakdowns. They're shipping specs in a day that used to take a week. The other hundred mostly use it to rewrite emails.\n\nPM: Why the gap?\nTom: The good ones figured it out alone and nobody else knows how. When I ask them to share, they send a forty-page prompt doc nobody reads. Knowledge doesn't spread.\n\nPM: What would help?\nTom: Show me which workflows produce real results, then package them so other teams can pick them up. A library of proven workflows, with the person who built it getting credit. Like an internal app store for how we work.\n\nPM: How would you know it's working?\nTom: Cycle time from discovery to approved spec, and how often engineering bounces a spec back. If those move, I don't care about logins.\n\nPM: Anything you'd avoid?\nTom: Leaderboards. The moment I rank PMs by AI usage, people will game it with junk prompts.\n"
